</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Pt1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part">Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experimental Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Hyperparameters and Resources</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameters.</span> To enable stochastic sampling from homogeneous agents, we set the sampling temperature to 1.0, and use nucleus sampling probability of 0.9, which means that sampling is done a dynamic set of likely tokens that together account for 90% of the total probability.
Furthermore, we generate a maximum of 512 tokens for all models experimented in the paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Resources.</span> All experiments were conducted using either RTX A6000 or RTX A100 GPUs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Dataset Details</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we provide dataset details and the number of samples utilized in our experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Arithmetics</span> comprises 100 arithmetic questions, in the form of “<span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">What is the result of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b*c+d-e/f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b*c+d-e/f</annotation></semantics></math>?</span>" The values <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> are randomly sampled from integers between 0 to 30.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GSM8K</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> comprises high-quality grade school math word problems intended to test mathematical multi-step reasoning.
We randomly subsample 300 questions from the original test split.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MMLU (Professional Medicine)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> is a benchmark specialized in evaluating reasoning abilities in medical domains at a professional level.
Specifically, the dataset requires medical concepts, clinical reasoning, and biomedical knowledge to answer questions.
We use the entire test split comprised of 272 questions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MMLU (Formal Logic)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> is designed to evaluate a model’s proficiency in formal reasoning, symbolic manipulation, and logical analysis.
We use the entire test split comprised of 126 question for evaluation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HellaSwag</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> is a natural language inference (NLI) benchmark dataset, in the context of sentence completion tasks.
That is, the benchmark tests whether a model can choose the most plausible continuation of a given context from multiple options, which is a task that demands not just linguistic proficiency but also real-world knowledge and reasoning.
We randomly subsample 300 questions from the original test split.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CommonsenseQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> is a multiple-choice question answering dataset designed to evaluate a model’s ability to apply commonsense knowledge in natural language understanding.
We randomly subsample 300 questions from the original validation split.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HH-RLHF</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> is a collection of human-annotated data designed to train and evaluate language models for alignment with human preferences, focusing on helpfulness and harmlessness.
The dataset is annotated with relative preferences, comprising ‘chosen’ and ‘rejected’ sample pairs.
Similar to the “AI labeler alignment” practice <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, we ask the LLM agent to select the example that is more helpful and less harmful.
To avoid selection bias <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>, we randomly shuffle the order of “chosen" and “rejected" in the input prompt.
We use a random subset of 300 pairs from the original test split.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CNN/DailyMails</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> is a dataset for abstractive text summarization.
It was originally constructed from news articles published by CNN and the Daily Mail, aimed for evaluating models that generate concise summaries of long-form text.
We use a random subset of 30 samples from the test split of dataset version 3.0.0.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Prompt Templates</h3>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we provide all the prompt templates used for our experiments.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>MAD Templates</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following is the prompt template for multi-agent debate.
For brevity, assume 3 agents are in the debate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These are the recent opinions from other agents:</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One of the agents’ response:</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;agent 2’s response from the previous round&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">One of the agents’ response:</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;agent 3’s response from the previous round&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This was your most recent opinion:</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;agent 1’s response from the previous round&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Use these opinions carefully as additional advice to revise your recent opinion to give your final answer to the question:</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;question&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Make sure to state your final answer in curly brackets at the very end of your response, just like: "{final answer: 12.34}".</span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For GSM8K, we give a slightly different demonstrative example: “{final answer: 123}", and for the other MCQ datasets, we give: “{final answer: (A)}".
For the CNN/Daily Mail dataset, we instruct the model to ‘Make sure to provide your summary after stating "# Summary #".’</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Task Templates</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we provide the exact input format used for each dataset.
These templates correspond to the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;question&gt;</span> field in the MAD prompt structure.
Datasets not listed below follow the original question format as provided in their respective sources without modification.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS2.p2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Arithmetics</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">What is the result of <math id="A2.SS2.p2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>+<math id="A2.SS2.p2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>*<math id="A2.SS2.p2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>+<math id="A2.SS2.p2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="A2.SS2.p2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math>÷<math id="A2.SS2.p2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>?</span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">MMLU Professional Medicine &amp; Formal Logic</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;question&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">(A) <span id="A2.SS2.p3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 1&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(B) <span id="A2.SS2.p3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 2&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(C) <span id="A2.SS2.p3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 3&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">(D) <span id="A2.SS2.p3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 4&gt;</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">HellaSwag</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Can you choose the option that best follows:</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">"<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;context&gt;</span>"?</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(A) <span id="A2.SS2.p4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 1&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(B) <span id="A2.SS2.p4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 2&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">(C) <span id="A2.SS2.p4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 3&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">(D) <span id="A2.SS2.p4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 4&gt;</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">CommonsenseQA</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;question&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">(A) <span id="A2.SS2.p5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 1&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(B) <span id="A2.SS2.p5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 2&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(C) <span id="A2.SS2.p5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 3&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">(D) <span id="A2.SS2.p5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 4&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">(E) <span id="A2.SS2.p5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;option 5&gt;</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS2.p6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">HH-RLHF</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Which of the following is relatively more helpful and/or harmless data?</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">(A) <span id="A2.SS2.p6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;chosen&gt;</span> <span id="A2.SS2.p6.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">or</span> <span id="A2.SS2.p6.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;rejected&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(B) <span id="A2.SS2.p6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;rejected&gt;</span> <span id="A2.SS2.p6.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">or</span> <span id="A2.SS2.p6.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;chosen&gt;</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS2.p7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">CNN/DailyMails</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Summarize the following in three sentences:</span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS2.p7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;article&gt;</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Persona Prompts</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assign heterogeneous personas to agents, we use a system prompt that specifies the role each agent should assume. We adopt the persona descriptions from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, which are provided below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Assistant</span>: You are a super-intelligent AI assistant capable of performing tasks more effectively than humans.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Mathematician</span>: You are a mathematician. You are good at math games, arithmetic calculation, and long-term planning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Economist</span>: You are an economist. You are good at economics, finance, and business. You have experience on understanding charts while interpreting the macroeconomic environment prevailing across world economies.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Programmer</span>: You are a programmer. You are good at computer science, engineering, and physics. You have experience in designing and developing computer software and hardware.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Lawyer</span>: You are a lawyer. You are good at law, politics, and history.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Psychologist</span>: You are a psychologist. You are good at psychology, sociology, and philosophy. You give people scientific suggestions that will make them feel better.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Doctor</span>: You are a doctor and come up with creative treatments for illnesses or diseases. You are able to recommend conventional medicines, herbal remedies and other natural alternatives. You also consider the patient’s age, lifestyle and medical history when providing your recommendations.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Special Case of Theorem 1</h3>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we analyze a special case of Theorem 1, where the probability of the correct answer, denoted by <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, exceeds <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In other words, each agent independently makes a correct decision with probability at least 0.5.
It naturally follows that <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\geq 1-\theta_{1}=\sum_{i=2}^{k}\theta_{i}\geq\max_{i\in\{2,\ldots,k\}}\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\geq 1-\theta_{1}=\sum_{i=2}^{k}\theta_{i}\geq\max_{i\in\{2,\ldots,k\}}\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that the margin term <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem 1 requires <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which does not rely on the number of agents <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> or the set size of possible answers <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To formalize this, we define <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}:=\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}:=\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to represent the initial probability that an individual agent selects the correct answer.
Also, for simplicity, let <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2},\ldots,X_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2},\ldots,X_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent Bernoulli random variables, where <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Bernoulli</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The average correctness across agents is then given by the empirical mean <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to the fraction of agents who vote correctly.
Under this setup, we analyze the lower bound of the Majority Voting success probability as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.A (Majority Voting Success Probability)</span>.
<span id="A3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2},\ldots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2},\ldots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent Bernoulli random variables with <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Bernoulli</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability that each agent is correct. Let <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the fraction of correct agents among <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> independent agents. If <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}&gt;\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}&gt;\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability that a majority vote is successful is lower bounded as follows:
</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\left(\bar{X}&gt;\frac{1}{2}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-2N\left(p_{0}-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\left(\bar{X}&gt;\frac{1}{2}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-2N\left(p_{0}-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem 1.A.</span>
Since <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Bernoulli</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[X_{i}]=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[X_{i}]=p</annotation></semantics></math>, and the variables are independent and bounded: <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq X_{i}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq X_{i}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[S_{n}]=np" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[S_{n}]=np</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}=\frac{S_{n}}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}=\frac{S_{n}}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[\bar{X}]=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[\bar{X}]=p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We apply Hoeffding’s Inequality to bound the deviation of <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> from its mean. Hoeffding’s Inequality states that for independent random variables <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\leq X_{i}\leq b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\leq X_{i}\leq b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(S_{n}-E[S_{n}]\geq t)\leq\exp\left(-\frac{2t^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(S_{n}-E[S_{n}]\geq t)\leq\exp\left(-\frac{2t^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(S_{n}-E[S_{n}]\leq-t)\leq\exp\left(-\frac{2t^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(S_{n}-E[S_{n}]\leq-t)\leq\exp\left(-\frac{2t^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}=n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\epsilon n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\epsilon n</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(S_{n}-np\leq-\epsilon n)\leq\exp\left(-\frac{2(\epsilon n)^{2}}{n}\right)=\exp(-2n\epsilon^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(S_{n}-np\leq-\epsilon n)\leq\exp\left(-\frac{2(\epsilon n)^{2}}{n}\right)=\exp(-2n\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Rewrite in terms of <math id="A3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(S_{n}-np\leq-\epsilon n)=P\left(\frac{S_{n}}{n}-p\leq-\epsilon\right)=P(\bar{X}\leq p-\epsilon)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(S_{n}-np\leq-\epsilon n)=P\left(\frac{S_{n}}{n}-p\leq-\epsilon\right)=P(\bar{X}\leq p-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\bar{X}\leq p-\epsilon)\leq\exp(-2n\epsilon^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\bar{X}\leq p-\epsilon)\leq\exp(-2n\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We want the majority vote to be successful, i.e., <math id="A3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}&gt;\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}&gt;\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p13.1" class="ltx_p">First, consider the complementary event:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\left(\bar{X}\leq\frac{1}{2}\right)=P\left(\bar{X}\leq p-\left(p-\frac{1}{2}\right)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\left(\bar{X}\leq\frac{1}{2}\right)=P\left(\bar{X}\leq p-\left(p-\frac{1}{2}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">and set <math id="A3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=p-\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=p-\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-\epsilon=\frac{1}{2}\implies\epsilon=p-\frac{1}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-\epsilon=\frac{1}{2}\implies\epsilon=p-\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Substitute <math id="A3.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\left(\bar{X}\leq\frac{1}{2}\right)\leq\exp\left(-2n\left(p-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\left(\bar{X}\leq\frac{1}{2}\right)\leq\exp\left(-2n\left(p-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p19.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the probability of a successful majority vote is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\left(\bar{X}&gt;\frac{1}{2}\right)=1-P\left(\bar{X}\leq\frac{1}{2}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-2n\left(p-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\left(\bar{X}&gt;\frac{1}{2}\right)=1-P\left(\bar{X}\leq\frac{1}{2}\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-2n\left(p-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Proof completed.
<math id="A3.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p22.1" class="ltx_p">Under this alternative formulation, the term <math id="A3.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> serves as a conservative approximation of the margin <math id="A3.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, since all competing answer choices are necessarily assigned probabilities less than <math id="A3.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, note that the dominant term in the resulting lower bound remains consistent with that of the orignal Theorem 1, scaling as <math id="A3.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N\cdot\Delta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N\cdot\Delta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs</h3>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1. (Majority Voting Success Probability)</span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=(\bar{\theta}^{(1)},\ldots,\bar{\theta}^{(K)})=\boldsymbol{\alpha}/\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝛉</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝛂</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=(\bar{\theta}^{(1)},\ldots,\bar{\theta}^{(K)})=\boldsymbol{\alpha}/\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the mean of the Dirichlet distribution, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Dirichlet</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the margin <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta:=\bar{\theta_{1}}-\bar{\theta_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta:=\bar{\theta_{1}}-\bar{\theta_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;k/\Delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;k/\Delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the probability that majority voting selects the answer 1 is lower bounded as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1)\geq 1-\exp\left(-N\left(\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{k}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1)\geq 1-\exp\left(-N\left(\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{k}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem 1.</span>
We proceed in several steps to establish the result.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Step 1: Define the Empirical Distribution</h4>

<div id="A4.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The empirical distribution of votes is given by <math id="A4.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{p}}=\mathbf{c}/N=(\hat{p}_{1},\hat{p}_{2},\ldots,\hat{p}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{p}}=\mathbf{c}/N=(\hat{p}_{1},\hat{p}_{2},\ldots,\hat{p}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{j}=c_{j}/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{j}=c_{j}/N</annotation></semantics></math> is the fraction of agents selecting answer <math id="A4.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. The true distribution is <math id="A4.SSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}=\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}=\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{p}_{j}]=\bar{\theta}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{p}_{j}]=\bar{\theta}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. The majority-voted answer corresponds to the index with the largest <math id="A4.SSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mathrm{mv}}=\underset{j\in\{1,\ldots,K\}}{\arg\max}\;\hat{p}_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mathrm{mv}}=\underset{j\in\{1,\ldots,K\}}{\arg\max}\;\hat{p}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to show that <math id="A4.SSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{1}&gt;\hat{p}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{1}&gt;\hat{p}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math> with high probability under the given conditions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Step 2: Establish a Key Lemma</h4>

<div id="A4.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To connect the empirical distribution to majority voting, we introduce the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SSx2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.</span> <span id="A4.SSx2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A4.SSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SSx2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SSx2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SSx2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Lemma 2.</span> We prove this by contrapositive. Suppose <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mathrm{mv}}\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mathrm{mv}}\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, there exists some <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{j}\geq\hat{p}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{j}\geq\hat{p}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Compute the <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm contribution involving classes 1 and <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1}|+|p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j}|\geq|(p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1})-(p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j})|=|p_{1}-p_{j}-(\hat{p}_{1}-\hat{p}_{j})|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1}|+|p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j}|\geq|(p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1})-(p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j})|=|p_{1}-p_{j}-(\hat{p}_{1}-\hat{p}_{j})|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}=\bar{\theta}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}=\bar{\theta}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}=\bar{\theta}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}=\bar{\theta}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\bar{\theta}_{1}-\bar{\theta}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\bar{\theta}_{1}-\bar{\theta}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and given <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}_{1}\geq\bar{\theta}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}_{1}\geq\bar{\theta}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}-p_{j}\geq\bar{\theta}_{1}-\bar{\theta}_{2}=\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}-p_{j}\geq\bar{\theta}_{1}-\bar{\theta}_{2}=\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}_{2}\geq\bar{\theta}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}_{2}\geq\bar{\theta}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>). Given <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{j}\geq\hat{p}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{j}\geq\hat{p}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, compute:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{1}-\hat{p}_{j}\leq 0\quad\text{and}\quad p_{1}-p_{j}\geq\Delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{1}-\hat{p}_{j}\leq 0\quad\text{and}\quad p_{1}-p_{j}\geq\Delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">so:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}-p_{j}-(\hat{p}_{1}-\hat{p}_{j})\geq\Delta-0=\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}-p_{j}-(\hat{p}_{1}-\hat{p}_{j})\geq\Delta-0=\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Thus:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1})-(p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j})|\geq\Delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1})-(p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j})|\geq\Delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">implying:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1}|+|p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j}|\geq\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1}|+|p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j}|\geq\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx2.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}|p_{i}-\hat{p}_{i}|\geq|p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1}|+|p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}|p_{i}-\hat{p}_{i}|\geq|p_{1}-\hat{p}_{1}|+|p_{j}-\hat{p}_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx2.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Hence, if <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mathrm{mv}}\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mathrm{mv}}\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Conversely, if <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Proof of Lemma 2 completed. <math id="A4.SSx2.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SSx2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This lemma implies:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1)\geq\mathbb{P}(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1)\geq\mathbb{P}(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Step 3: Bound the <math id="A4.SSx3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> Deviation</h4>

<div id="A4.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=\boldsymbol{\alpha}/\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝜶</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}=\boldsymbol{\alpha}/\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the mean of the categorical distribution induced by the Dirichlet model, and agents draw answers independently from <math id="A4.SSx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the counts <math id="A4.SSx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}\sim\mathrm{Multinomial}(N,\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Multinomial</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}\sim\mathrm{Multinomial}(N,\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that the Dirichlet-multinomial assumption in the original proof simplifies to a multinomial distribution here because <math id="A4.SSx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed as the mean.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We need to bound <math id="A4.SSx3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>. We use a concentration inequality for multinomial distributions. A known result (e.g., Proposition 19 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>) provides:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\sqrt{K}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}+\epsilon\right)\right)\leq\exp(-N\epsilon^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\sqrt{K}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}+\epsilon\right)\right)\leq\exp(-N\epsilon^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="A4.SSx3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This bound accounts for the <math id="A4.SSx3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional nature of the distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Set the threshold equal to <math id="A4.SSx3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{K}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}+\epsilon\right)=\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{K}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}+\epsilon\right)=\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Solve for <math id="A4.SSx3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}+\epsilon=\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}+\epsilon=\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">The condition <math id="A4.SSx3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;K/\Delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;K/\Delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures <math id="A4.SSx3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}&gt;\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\quad\text{implies}\quad\sqrt{N}\Delta&gt;\sqrt{K}\quad\text{or}\quad N\Delta^{2}&gt;K," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>implies</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}&gt;\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\quad\text{implies}\quad\sqrt{N}\Delta&gt;\sqrt{K}\quad\text{or}\quad N\Delta^{2}&gt;K,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">which matches the theorem’s condition. Since <math id="A4.SSx3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, this condition guarantees the bound is meaningful.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SSx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Substitute <math id="A4.SSx3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> into the inequality:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\Delta\right)\leq\exp\left(-N\left(\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}\geq\Delta\right)\leq\exp\left(-N\left(\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Thus:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-N\left(\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta\right)\geq 1-\exp\left(-N\left(\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SSx4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Step 4: Conclusion</h4>

<div id="A4.SSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Lemma 2:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1)\geq\mathbb{P}(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1)\geq\mathbb{P}(\|\hat{\mathbf{p}}-\mathbf{p}\|_{1}&lt;\Delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Combining with the probability bound, we derive:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1)\geq 1-\exp\left(-N\left(\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>mv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y_{\mathrm{mv}}=1)\geq 1-\exp\left(-N\left(\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{K}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SSx4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This matches the statement of Theorem 1. Proof completed. <math id="A4.SSx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof of Lemma 1</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1. (Bayesian Conjugacy in Multi-Agent Debate)</span>
<span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">At round <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, after observing responses from its neighbors <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>, the agent <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> aggregates these into a count vector <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition 2. Then, by Bayesian conjugacy, the posterior distribution over <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛉</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> remains Dirichlet:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\sim\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}+\mathbf{c}_{i,t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Dirichlet</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\sim\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}+\mathbf{c}_{i,t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Lemma 1.</span>
We aim to show that the posterior distribution of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the agent <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s belief over the answer space at round <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, given the observed responses <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> from its neighbors, is a Dirichlet distribution with updated parameters <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}+\mathbf{c}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}+\mathbf{c}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">First, consider the prior belief of agent <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> at the start of round <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, which is based on its belief from the previous round <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math>. The prior distribution over the parameter <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\sim\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)},\ldots,\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(K)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Dirichlet</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\sim\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)},\ldots,\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(K)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}=(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)},\ldots,\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(K)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}=(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)},\ldots,\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(K)})</annotation></semantics></math> are positive real numbers representing the prior parameters inherited from the previous round, and the density is proportional to:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t})\propto\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(m)}-1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∝</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t})\propto\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(m)}-1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">At round <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, agent <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> observes the responses <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> from its neighbors, where <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j,t-1}\in\{1,\ldots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j,t-1}\in\{1,\ldots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the answer chosen by neighbor <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> at round <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math>. According to Definition 2, these responses are aggregated into a count vector <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}_{i,t}=(c_{i,t}^{(1)},\ldots,c_{i,t}^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}_{i,t}=(c_{i,t}^{(1)},\ldots,c_{i,t}^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math>, where:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{i,t}^{(m)}=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\mathbf{1}[y_{j,t-1}=m]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i,t}^{(m)}=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\mathbf{1}[y_{j,t-1}=m],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=1}^{k}c_{i,t}^{(m)}=|\mathcal{N}(i)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=1}^{k}c_{i,t}^{(m)}=|\mathcal{N}(i)|</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of neighbors. Assuming each neighbor’s response <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j,t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j,t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn independently from a categorical distribution parameterized by <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the likelihood of observing the count vector <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a multinomial distribution:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}_{i,t}\mid\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\sim\text{Multinomial}(|\mathcal{N}(i)|,\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Multinomial</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}_{i,t}\mid\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\sim\text{Multinomial}(|\mathcal{N}(i)|,\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">with the likelihood proportional to:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{c}_{i,t}\mid\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t})\propto\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{c_{i,t}^{(m)}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∝</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{c}_{i,t}\mid\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t})\propto\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{c_{i,t}^{(m)}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By Bayesian conjugacy, the posterior distribution of <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> given the observed counts is proportional to the product of the prior and the likelihood:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{c}_{i,t})\propto p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t})\cdot p(\mathbf{c}_{i,t}\mid\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{c}_{i,t})\propto p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t})\cdot p(\mathbf{c}_{i,t}\mid\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting the expressions:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{c}_{i,t})\propto\left(\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(m)}-1}}\right)\cdot\left(\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{c_{i,t}^{(m)}}}\right)=\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(m)}+c_{i,t}^{(m)}-1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{c}_{i,t})\propto\left(\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(m)}-1}}\right)\cdot\left(\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{c_{i,t}^{(m)}}}\right)=\prod_{m=1}^{K}\theta_{i,t}^{(m)^{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(m)}+c_{i,t}^{(m)}-1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">This form is characteristic of a Dirichlet distribution. Thus, the posterior is:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\sim\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+c_{i,t}^{(1)},\ldots,\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(K)}+c_{i,t}^{(K)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Dirichlet</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\sim\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+c_{i,t}^{(1)},\ldots,\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(K)}+c_{i,t}^{(K)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p">or equivalently:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\sim\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}+\mathbf{c}_{i,t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Dirichlet</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{i,t}\mid\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\sim\mathrm{Dirichlet}(\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}+\mathbf{c}_{i,t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is derived from the neighbor responses <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{j,t-1}\}_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> as specified, and the update follows from the conjugacy property of the Dirichlet and multinomial distributions, the lemma holds. Proof completed. <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proof of Theorem 2</h4>

<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate)</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any agent <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> at round <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, if</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}(i)|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}p_{j,t-1}=p_{i,t-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}(i)|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}p_{j,t-1}=p_{i,t-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then sequence <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i,t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i,t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a martingale. That is, the expected belief at the next round equals the current belief:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\mid\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{t-1}]=p_{i,t-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\mid\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{t-1}]=p_{i,t-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem 2.</span>
For agent <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with neighbors <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,t}:=\bar{{\theta}}_{i,t}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,t}:=\bar{{\theta}}_{i,t}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote its belief in the correct answer at debate round <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Bayesian conjugacy,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,t}:=\bar{\theta}_{i,t}^{(1)}=\frac{\alpha_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t}^{(j)}}=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+c_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+c_{i,t}^{(j)})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,t}:=\bar{\theta}_{i,t}^{(1)}=\frac{\alpha_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t}^{(j)}}=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+c_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+c_{i,t}^{(j)})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here, we prove that the sequence <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i,t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i,t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale by showing that the conditional expectation of the belief in the correct answer at round <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> given the filtration up to round <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math> equals the current belief.
A sequence <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale if <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{t}\mid\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]=X_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{t}\mid\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]=X_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t-1}=(\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{0},\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1},\cdots,\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t-1}=(\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{0},\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1},\cdots,\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the history of belief parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By definition, we can write an agent’s belief in the correct answer at timestep <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{i,t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{i,t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+c_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+c_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i,t}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i,t}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of neighboring agents that has selected the correct answer at the previous debate round.
Then, the expectation of <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on the filtration <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+c_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+c_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\mathbb{E}[c_{i,t}^{(1)}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\mathbb{E}[c_{i,t}^{(1)}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\mathbb{E}[\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\mathbf{1}\{y_{j,t-1}=1\}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\mathbb{E}[\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\mathbf{1}\{y_{j,t-1}=1\}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}p_{j,t-1}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}p_{j,t-1}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|\,p_{i,t-1}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}\qquad\text{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}(by the condition in Theorem 2)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>(by the condition in Theorem 2)</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|\,p_{i,t-1}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+|\mathcal{N}(i)|}\qquad\text{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}(by the condition in Theorem 2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">From equation (<a href="#A4.E2" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem 2 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Appendix ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}=p_{i,t-1}\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}=p_{i,t-1}\sum_{j=1}^{K}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">and by plugging equation (<a href="#A4.E9" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem 2 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Appendix ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) into equation (<a href="#A4.E8" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem 2 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Appendix ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), we arrive at</p>
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]=p_{i,t-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]=p_{i,t-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Proof completed. <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.1 </span>When does (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) in Theorem 2 Hold?</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order for a multi-agent debate to be a martingale process, the condition in Theorem 2, equation (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),
which states the relation between the belief of an agent with its peers’ beliefs, should hold.
Here, we expand our discussion to exploring debate topologies that satisfy (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), therefore the martingale property.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proposition 1. (Sufficient Conditions for (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>))</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If the debate topology consists of agents that either (i) are homogeneous and fully-connected, or (ii) are fully-isolated, or (iii) form isolated cliques whose agents in each clique are homogeneous, then the debate process is a martingale.
</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">proof of Proposition 1.</span>
We prove one by one that each case satisfies (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">(i) Homogeneous agents with fully-connected communication topology</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This setting best represents our core experimental setting: Decentralized MAD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>.
In this setup, since the agents are homogeneous, their initial beliefs are identical: <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}=\cdots=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{n,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}=\cdots=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{n,0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, since we are assuming a fully-connected communication topology, the count vector <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{c}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{c}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> that counts the neighboring agents’ answers (including itself), is identical across agents.
Therefore, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t}=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}+\boldsymbol{c}_{i,t}=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i^{\prime},t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒄</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t}=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i,t-1}+\boldsymbol{c}_{i,t}=\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{i^{\prime},t}</annotation></semantics></math> holds for all <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,i^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,i^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By dividing the equation with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{\cdot,t}||_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{\cdot,t}||_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{i,t}=p_{i^{\prime},t}\;\forall_{i,i^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,t}=p_{i^{\prime},t}\;\forall_{i,i^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is satisfied. <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(ii) Fully-isolated structure with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(i)=\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(i)=\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This is an extreme case where none of the agent is connected to a peer.
That is, an agent will only refer to its own previous answer to update its response, which is effectively an iterative self-refinement approach.
In this case, each agent’s belief parameter evolves independently through <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{i,t}=\alpha_{i,t-1}+\mathbf{1}\{y_{i,t-1}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,t}=\alpha_{i,t-1}+\mathbf{1}\{y_{i,t-1}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where without loss of generality, answer 1 is the correct answer.
Hence, it can be easily shown that each agent follows a martingale process, satisfying (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
Note that this holds regardless of the homogeneity and heterogeneity of the agents. <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">(iii) Isolated cliques, where agents in a clique are homogeneous</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">This scenario is a mixture of the above two cases.
Within each clique, the agents’ belief vectors evolve with respect to case 1 above.
Then, the entire topology of multiple cliques will follow case 2, where each clique’s collective belief evolves independently of other cliques.
Hence, as a whole, (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is satisfied. <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">In all three cases (i)-(iii), (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is satisfied.
Then, by Theorem 2, a multi-agent debate system with debate topologies equivalent to (i)-(iii) will have the martingale property. <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark 2.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition 1 provides several sufficient conditions under which equation (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) holds.
There may, however, exist other debate graph topologies that also satisfy this condition.
A complete characterization of such cases is left for future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.2 </span>When does (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) in Theorem 2 <span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Not</span> hold?</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to the cases where the condition in Theorem 2 hold, it is also important to examine the debate topologies under which (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) does not hold.
Here, we discuss two cases: line graph and ring graph.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">1. Line graph</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A debate topology that consists of three agents connected as a line may not satisfy (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), as shown below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="14.39" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 171.87 14.39" width="171.87"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,14.39) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(7.2,0) translate(0,7.2)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 6.92 0 C 6.92 3.82 3.82 6.92 0 6.92 C -3.82 6.92 -6.92 3.82 -6.92 0 C -6.92 -3.82 -3.82 -6.92 0 -6.92 C 3.82 -6.92 6.92 -3.82 6.92 0 Z M 0 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.46 -4.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text">1</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 85.66 0 C 85.66 3.82 82.56 6.92 78.74 6.92 C 74.92 6.92 71.82 3.82 71.82 0 C 71.82 -3.82 74.92 -6.92 78.74 -6.92 C 82.56 -6.92 85.66 -3.82 85.66 0 Z M 78.74 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 75.28 -4.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic1.2" class="ltx_text">2</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 164.4 0 C 164.4 3.82 161.3 6.92 157.48 6.92 C 153.66 6.92 150.56 3.82 150.56 0 C 150.56 -3.82 153.66 -6.92 157.48 -6.92 C 161.3 -6.92 164.4 -3.82 164.4 0 Z M 157.48 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 154.02 -4.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic1.3" class="ltx_text">3</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 7.2 0 L 71.54 0"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 85.94 0 L 150.29 0"></path></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let the agents be homogeneous and their initial beliefs in the correct answer be <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\alpha}_{1,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{2,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{3,0}^{(1)}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\alpha}_{1,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{2,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{3,0}^{(1)}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{3,0}||_{1}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{3,0}||_{1}=2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the count vector <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is randomly generated, it could happen that <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=(1,0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=(1,0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This means only agent 1 produced the correct answer.
In terms of Dirichlet parameter updates, we have:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{1,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}||_{1}+2}=\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{1,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}||_{1}+2}=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{2,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{2,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{2,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{2}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{2,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{2}{5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{3,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{3,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{3,0}^{(1)}}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{3,0}||_{1}+2}=\frac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{3,0}^{(1)}}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{3,0}||_{1}+2}=\frac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">In this case, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{2,1}\neq\frac{1}{3}\left(p_{1,1}+p_{2,1}+p_{3,1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{2,1}\neq\frac{1}{3}\left(p_{1,1}+p_{2,1}+p_{3,1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, this serves as a counterexample to condition (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) for future time steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2. Ring graph</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">A debate topology that consists of four agents forming a ring graph may not satisfy (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), as shown below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="93.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 93.13 93.13" width="93.13"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,93.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(7.2,0) translate(0,7.2)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 6.92 0 C 6.92 3.82 3.82 6.92 0 6.92 C -3.82 6.92 -6.92 3.82 -6.92 0 C -6.92 -3.82 -3.82 -6.92 0 -6.92 C 3.82 -6.92 6.92 -3.82 6.92 0 Z M 0 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.46 -4.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic2.1" class="ltx_text">1</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 85.66 0 C 85.66 3.82 82.56 6.92 78.74 6.92 C 74.92 6.92 71.82 3.82 71.82 0 C 71.82 -3.82 74.92 -6.92 78.74 -6.92 C 82.56 -6.92 85.66 -3.82 85.66 0 Z M 78.74 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 75.28 -4.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic2.2" class="ltx_text">2</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 85.66 78.74 C 85.66 82.56 82.56 85.66 78.74 85.66 C 74.92 85.66 71.82 82.56 71.82 78.74 C 71.82 74.92 74.92 71.82 78.74 71.82 C 82.56 71.82 85.66 74.92 85.66 78.74 Z M 78.74 78.74"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 75.28 74.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic2.3" class="ltx_text">3</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 6.92 78.74 C 6.92 82.56 3.82 85.66 0 85.66 C -3.82 85.66 -6.92 82.56 -6.92 78.74 C -6.92 74.92 -3.82 71.82 0 71.82 C 3.82 71.82 6.92 74.92 6.92 78.74 Z M 0 78.74"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.46 74.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS2.pic2.4" class="ltx_text">4</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 7.2 0 L 71.54 0"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 78.74 7.2 L 78.74 71.54"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 71.54 78.74 L 7.2 78.74"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 71.54 L 0 7.2"></path></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Let the agents be homogeneous and their initial beliefs in the correct answer be <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\alpha}_{1,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{2,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{3,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{4,0}^{(1)}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\alpha}_{1,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{2,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{3,0}^{(1)}={\alpha}_{4,0}^{(1)}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{3,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{4,0}||_{1}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{3,0}||_{1}=||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{4,0}||_{1}=2</annotation></semantics></math>.
If only agent 1 got the answer correct at <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{1,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{2}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{1,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{1,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{2}{5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{2,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{2,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{2,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{2}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{2,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{2,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{2}{5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{3,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{3,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{3,0}^{(1)}}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{3,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{1}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{3,0}^{(1)}}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{3,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{1}{5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{4,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{4,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{4,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{4,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{2}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\alpha}_{4,0}^{(1)}+1}{||\boldsymbol{\alpha}_{4,0}||_{1}+3}=\frac{2}{5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{3,1}\neq\frac{1}{3}\left(p_{2,1}+p_{3,1}+p_{4,1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{3,1}\neq\frac{1}{3}\left(p_{2,1}+p_{3,1}+p_{4,1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, this serves as a counterexample to (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
Notably, this ring graph corresponds to the Sparse MAD baseline <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.
Although this topology does not theoretically guarantee the martingale property, we empirically demonstrate in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Martingale Process Empirical Investigation ‣ Appendix ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> that it holds approximately.
We conjecture that the dynamics for short debate rounds does not deviate greatly from a martingale.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Collective Intelligence</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the agents are heterogeneous and fully-connected, the debate is not necessarily a martingale since the condition (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 2. (Martingale Behavior of Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) for individual agent beliefs may not hold.
However, we find that the "collective intelligence" may follow a martingale.
Let’s define the collective belief of the correct answer as:</p>
<table id="A4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}:=\frac{\sum_{i}\alpha_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{i,k}\alpha_{i,t}^{(k)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}:=\frac{\sum_{i}\alpha_{i,t}^{(1)}}{\sum_{i,k}\alpha_{i,t}^{(k)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then, the expected collective belief is:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[q_{t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[q_{t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i}\left(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\mathbb{E}[c_{i,t}^{(1)}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]\right)}{\sum_{i,k}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(k)}+\sum_{i}|\mathcal{N}(i)|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i}\left(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\mathbb{E}[c_{i,t}^{(1)}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]\right)}{\sum_{i,k}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(k)}+\sum_{i}|\mathcal{N}(i)|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i}\left(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\mathbb{E}[\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\mathbf{1}\{y_{j,t-1}=1\}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]\right)}{\sum_{i,k}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+\sum_{i}|\mathcal{N}(i)|}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i}\left(\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}+\mathbb{E}[\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\mathbf{1}\{y_{j,t-1}=1\}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]\right)}{\sum_{i,k}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(j)}+\sum_{i}|\mathcal{N}(i)|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This collective belief will be a martingale if and only if</p>
<table id="A4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{i}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}\{y_{j,t-1}=1\}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t}]}{\sum_{i}|\mathcal{N}(i)|}=q_{t-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{i}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}\{y_{j,t-1}=1\}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t}]}{\sum_{i}|\mathcal{N}(i)|}=q_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">is satisfied in (<a href="#A4.E20" title="In D.4 Collective Intelligence ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Appendix ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).
This condition is equivalent to</p>
<table id="A4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{i}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}p_{j,t-1}}{\sum_{i}|\mathcal{N}(i)|}=\frac{\sum_{i}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}}{\sum_{i,k}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(k)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{i}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(i)}p_{j,t-1}}{\sum_{i}|\mathcal{N}(i)|}=\frac{\sum_{i}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(1)}}{\sum_{i,k}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(k)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Then, a sufficient condition for this to hold is, for all <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\sum_{k}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(k)}=\text{Constant},\\
|\mathcal{N}(i)|=n,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Constant</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\sum_{k}\alpha_{i,t-1}^{(k)}=\text{Constant},\\
|\mathcal{N}(i)|=n,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">meaning that the magnitude of the belief vector should be constant across agents, and that all agents should be connected to each other.
When these conditions are met, <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a martingale process.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Martingale Process Empirical Investigation</h3>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we provide the raw mean accuracy values used for Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Lemma 1. (Bayesian Conjugacy in Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is provided in Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix E Martingale Process Empirical Investigation ‣ Appendix ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As further investigation, we directly evaluate the martingale process by comparing the <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, as measured by the mean accuracy values across agents at step <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math>, with the expected value of the next step <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]</annotation></semantics></math>, which is measured by running 5 independent runs on the subsequent debate round.
In the following two tables, we report the results with Sparse MAD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, consisting of Qwen2.5-7B agents and Llama3.1-8B agents, on three rounds of debate evaluated on the Formal Logic benchmark.
We observe that <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,t-1}\approx\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,t-1}\approx\mathbb{E}[p_{i,t}\;|\;\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> in both cases.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A5.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Raw mean accuracy values for Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Lemma 1. (Bayesian Conjugacy in Multi-Agent Debate) ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Debate or Vote: Which Yields Better Decisionsin Multi-Agent Large Language Models?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Top row is from Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, and the bottom row is from Llama3.1-8B-Instruct. The MAD structure is the fully connected Decentralized MAD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>.</span></figcaption>
<div id="A5.T6.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:327.8pt;height:87.4pt;vertical-align:-42.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-109.9pt,29.3pt) scale(0.598618454138471,0.598618454138471) ;">
<table id="A5.T6.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T6.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T6.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">Rounds</td>
<td id="A5.T6.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T6.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Arithmetics</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T6.5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GSM8K</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.5.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T6.5.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pro. Med.</span></td>
